  (text "RHD2164 DECOUPLING (PER IC) - CRITICAL
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Pin         Cap Value    Package   Rail         Placement
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VDD1        100nF        0402      AVDD         <2mm from pin, via to L3 plane
VDD2        100nF        0402      AVDD         <2mm from pin, via to L3 plane
VDD3        100nF        0402      AVDD         <2mm from pin, via to L3 plane
VDD_bulk    10µF         0603      AVDD         Near IC, shared for all VDD

VDDD1       100nF        0402      DVDD_AFE     <2mm from pin, via to L5 plane
VDDD2       100nF        0402      DVDD_AFE     <2mm from pin, via to L5 plane
VDDD_bulk   10µF         0603      DVDD_AFE     Near IC, shared for all VDDD

VREF        10µF         0603      (output)     Reference output, low ESR
AUXIN       NC           -         -            Not used

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NOTE: Place decoupling caps on BOTTOM layer directly under IC.
      Via to ground plane adjacent to each cap.
      Do NOT share ground vias between analog and digital caps.
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20 140)
    (effects
      (font (size 1.1 1.1))
      (justify left)
    )
  )

  (text "RHD2164 REGISTER CONFIGURATION (Firmware Reference)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Register  Value   Description
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
0         0xDE    ADC config: 30 kS/s, normal operation
1-2       ---     Bandwidth: 300 Hz HPF, 6000 Hz LPF (spike band)
3         0x00    MUX load, temp sensor, digital output
4         0x80    weakMiso=1 (MISO weakly driven when CS inactive)
5         0x00    Impedance check disabled
7         0x00    Impedance check channel select
8-13      ---     Bandwidth resistor DAC values (set by firmware)
14-17     0xFF    On-chip amps enabled (all 64 channels)
18-21     0xFF    Amps 32-63 power (visible on MISO_B only)

IDENTIFICATION (ROM registers, read-only):
  Reg 59: 53 on MISO_A, 58 on MISO_B (identifies RHD2164)
  Reg 60: Intan chip ID
  Reg 63: Intan company ID (should return 0x49 = 'I')

SAMPLE TIMING (DDR SPI — corrected from Rev 1.0):
  • 33.33 µs per sample (30 kS/s)
  • 35 SPI commands per sample period (32 CONVERT + 3 AUX)
  • Each command: 16 bits on MOSI, 16 bits on each MISO
  • At 20 MHz SCLK: 35 × 16/20MHz = 28.0 µs per chip
  • With parallel CS (2 buses): both chips read in 28.0 µs ✅
  • Margin: 33.33 - 28.0 = 5.33 µs (16% idle)

DATA FORMAT:
  • 16-bit unsigned offset (default) or two's complement
  • LSB = 0.195 µV (with default gain)
  • Full scale: ±6.4 mV
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"
